      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 10: is São Paulo's ε a braking-driven quantity? (no — it's a constant)",
      "text": "Refuted: no stop-go/braking predictor explains the per-ride gap (R² ≤ 0.07, two wrong-signed; the mechanistic correction over-corrects, RMS 0.19 vs flat-constant 0.08). Braking is invisible to ε because gravity re-supplies the braked-away speed on a descent — so ε ≈ 0.20 as a constant, and the rural −0.13 offset transfers to São Paulo essentially unchanged.",
      "appearance": [
        {
          "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/journal/MODEL_COMPARISON_JOURNAL.md"
        }
      ],
      "subjectOf": {
        "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/notes/claims.ttl"
      }
    },
